'''Mythical Island''' (Japanese: '''幻のいる島''' ''Illusory Island'') is the second expansion of cards, and first themed booster pack, in [[Pokémon Trading Card Game Pocket]].

== Information ==
[[File:AerodactylexMythicalIsland84 artwork.png|thumb|right|200px|Mythical Island as seen on {{TCG ID|Mythical Island|Aerodactyl ex|84}}]]
'''Mythical Island''' is the first themed booster pack released through [[Pokémon Trading Card Game Pocket]]. With a tropical island setting, this expansion focuses on [[Mythical Pokémon]] such as {{p|Mew}} and {{p|Celebi}}, which appear as {{TCGP|Pokémon ex}}. More characters from [[Generation I]] also make their card debuts in this expansion. In total, Mythical Island contains 86 cards, including five new Pokémon ex and five new Trainer cards; it also marks the first appearance of Pokémon from Generations {{gen|II}} and {{gen|IV}} in the game.

Many of the expansion's [[#Themed Collections|Themed Collections]] allude to locations around the island, and several of the new illustrations featured within them—including {{TCG ID|Mythical Island|Joltik|28}}, {{TCG ID|Mythical Island|Stonjourner|48}}, {{TCG ID|Mythical Island|Weezing|50}}, and {{TCG ID|Mythical Island|Chatot|62}}—feature cameos from Mew, as does the immersive illustration for {{TCG ID|Mythical Island|Celebi ex|3}}.

Mythical Island was released worldwide on December 17, 2024.

=== Setting ===
The island can be seen from above in {{TCG ID|Mythical Island|Aerodactyl ex|84|Aerodactyl ex}}'s special illustration rare. Areas called Untouched Forest, Tranquil Lake, Scorching Wilderness, Forgotten Ruins, and Tree of Repose are depicted in the cards that make up their respective Themed Collections as well as in the cover art unlocked as a reward for completing them. There may also be an unnamed settlement as depicted in the illustration rares of {{TCG ID|Mythical Island|Dedenne|73}} and {{TCG ID|Mythical Island|Marshadow|74}}.

